[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Crystal Palace]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.28]How many people visited the Great Exhibition of 1851? | 有多少人参观了1851年的万国博览会？
[00:18.20]Perhaps the most extraordinary building of the 19th century was the Crystal Palace | 19世纪最不寻常的建筑也许要数水晶宫了，
[00:26.04]which was built in Hyde Park for the Great Exhibition of 1851. | 它是为1851年的世界博览会而在海德公园建造的。
[00:33.43]The Crystal Palace was different from all other buildings in the world, for it was made of iron and glass. | 水晶宫不同于世界上所有的其他建筑，因为它是用铁和玻璃建成的。
[00:43.01]It was one of the biggest buildings of all time and a lot of people from many countries came to see it. | 它是有史以来最大的建筑之一，因此许多国家的人们都前来参观。
[00:52.23]A great many goods were sent to the exhibition from various parts of the world. | 大量的展品从世界各地运送到了博览会上。
[00:58.38]There was also a great deal of machinery on display. | 参展的还有很多机器。
[01:03.67]The most wonderful piece of machinery on show was Nasmyth's steam hammer. | 其中最奇妙的是内史密斯的蒸汽锤。
[01:11.50]Though in those days travelling was not as easy as it is today, | 尽管当时旅行不像现在这么容易，
[01:17.79]steam boats carried thousands of visitors across the Channel from Europe. | 蒸汽船还是把成千上万的参观者从欧洲大陆送过了英吉利海峡。
[01:23.94]On arriving in England, they were, taken to the Crystal Palace by train. | 一到英国，他们就乘火车被送往水晶宫。
[01:30.34]There were six million visitors in all, | 参观人数总计600万，
[01:33.91]and the profits from the exhibition were used to build museums and colleges. | 博览会的盈利被用来建造博物馆和大学。
[01:39.94]Later, the Crystal Palace was moved to South London. | 后来，水晶宫被移到了伦敦南郊。
[01:44.67]It remained one of the most famous buildings in the world until it was burnt down in 1936. | 直到1936年被烧毁为止，它一直是世界上最著名的建筑之一。
